  "description": "The WHEN OTHER arm of EVALUATE EIBAID at :190-194, reached with DFHPF5 - a key this program names in neither of its two arms. :191 raises WS-ERR-FLG, :192 moves -1 into MONTHLYL, :193 moves CCDA-MSG-INVALID-KEY (app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy, PIC X(50)) into WS-MESSAGE PIC X(80) and :194 sends. MONTHLYI travelled as 'Y' and is echoed back untouched, because this arm blanks nothing - proving the received map really is the buffer that is re-sent. Expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED by reading app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl, its copybooks, app/bms/CORPT00.bms and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD - never captured from a COBOL run, which is impossible in this environment (risk R-A). Java has no transient data queue, so EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') at :517 is reproduced through an explicit job-submission port; the eighty-byte content is identical and the dataset key JOBS names the TDQUEUE(JOBS) that app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:499-505 defines as RECORDSIZE(80) RECORDFORMAT(FIXED) BLOCKFORMAT(UNBLOCKED) DISPOSITION(MOD).",
